etSelectionFromTop()`. Both approaches work, but I'll go with the simpler `getFirstVisiblePosition()` and `getTop()` combination since it's more straightforward to implement and doesn't require calculating pixel offsets manually.\n\nNow I need to check if `loadArchive()` has the same scroll reset issue. Looking at that method, it also creates a new adapter and sets it on the list view, so yes—it has the same problem and needs the same fix applied to preserve the scroll position there as well.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
