{"type":"assistant","uuid":"c4afd922-038b-4d4c-8819-98699797cf28","session_id":"d7638cdb-eede-4644-bfaf-47b52fc19848","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"c4afd922-038b-4d4c-8819-98699797cf28","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The changes are confirmed. Let me now produce the final output patch for the user. I'll generate a unified diff that shows the changes from the original code to the fixed code.\n\nLet me summarize what I've done and present the patch.\n\nThe fix:\n\nIn `loadDirectory()`:\n- **Before**: Directly created new adapter and set it, which resets scroll to top\n- **After**: Saves scroll position (first visible item + offset) before creating adapter, restores it after setting adapter\n\nIn `loadArchive()`:\n- **Before**: Directly created new adapter and set it, which resets scroll to top\n- **After**: Saves scroll position before creating adapter, restores it after setting adapter\n\nThe patch output:\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"56c46606-39e7-4501-8b36-16f4e4cb48e9","session_id":"d7638cdb-eede-4644-bfaf-47b52fc19848","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"56c46606-39e7-4501-8b36-16f4e4cb48e9","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe fix has been successfully applied and verified by the build. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Bug Fix Summary\n\n**File:** `app/src/main/java/io/lerk/lrkFM/activities/FileActivity.java`\n\n**Root Cause:** Both `loadDirectory()` and `loadArchive()` methods create a **new** `ArrayAdapter` and call `fileListView.setAdapter()` every time the directory is reloaded (e.g., after file operations). Setting a new adapter resets the ListView's scroll position to the top (position 0, offset 0).\n\n**Fix:** Save the scroll position before reloading and restore it after setting the new adapter.\n\n### Patch:\n\n```diff\n--- a/app/src/main/java/io/lerk/lrkFM/activities/FileActivity.java\n+++ b/app/src/main/java/io/lerk/lrkFM/activities/FileActivity.java\n@@ -604,6 +604,12 @@\n         FileLoader fileLoader = new FileLoader(path);\n         View errorText = findViewById(R.id.unableToLoadText);\n         View emptyText = findViewById(R.id.emptyDirText);\n+\n+        // Save scroll position before reloading so we can restore it after\n+        int scrollPosition = fileListView.getFirstVisiblePosition();\n+        View v = fileListView.getChildAt(0);\n+        int scrollOffset = (v == null) ? 0 : v.getTop();\n+\n         try {\n             files = fileLoader.loadLocationFiles();\n             fileListView.setVisibility(VISIBLE);\n@@ -612,6 +618,9 @@\n \n             arrayAdapter = new FileArrayAdapter(this, R.layout.layout_file, sortFilesByPreference(files, new PrefUtils<String>(SORT_FILES_BY).getValue()));\n             fileListView.setAdapter(arrayAdapter);\n+\n+            // Restore scroll position after setting the new adapter\n+            fileListView.setSelectionFromTop(scrollPosition, scrollOffset);\n         } catch (NoAccessException e) {\n             Log.w(TAG, \"Can't read '\" + path + \"': Permission denied!\");\n             fileListView.setVisibility(GONE);\n@@ -650,6 +659,12 @@\n         View errorText = findViewById(R.id.unableToLoadText);\n         View emptyText = findViewById(R.id.emptyDirText);\n \n+        // Save scroll position before reloading so we can restore it after\n+        int scrollPosition = fileListView.getFirstVisiblePosition();\n+        View v = fileListView.getChildAt(0);\n+        int scrollOffset = (v == null) ? 0 : v.getTop();\n+\n         files = loader.loadLocationFiles();\n         fileListView.setVisibility(VISIBLE);\n         errorText.setVisibility(GONE);\n@@ -657,6 +672,9 @@\n \n         arrayAdapter = new ArchiveArrayAdapter(this, R.layout.layout_file, sortFilesByPreference(files, new PrefUtils<String>(SORT_FILES_BY).getValue()), archive);\n         fileListView.setAdapter(arrayAdapter);\n+\n+        // Restore scroll position after setting the new adapter\n+        fileListView.setSelectionFromTop(scrollPosition, scrollOffset);\n \n         currentDirectory = path;\n         historyMap.put(historyCounter++, new HistoryEntry(currentDirectory, archive));\n```\n\n**How it works:**\n1. **Save:** Before creating the new adapter, capture `getFirstVisiblePosition()` (the index of the topmost visible item) and `getChildAt(0).getTop()` (the pixel offset of that item from the top of the ListView)\n2. **Restore:** After `setAdapter()` is called, use `setSelectionFromTop(scrollPosition, scrollOffset)` to reposition the list to approximately the same location\n\nThis approach handles both normal scrolling (where the top item may be partially visible) and edge cases (first item at position 0 with no offset). The fix applies to both regular directories (`loadDirectory`) and archive browsing (`loadArchive`)."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":43607,"output_tokens":988,"cache_read_input_tokens":42752,"total_tokens":44595}}}
